        "execSummary":  "The article\u0027s central finding—that AI-native teams achieve 4.5x to 10x productivity gains through workflow redesign, not just tool adoption—has direct implications for any organization planning an AI transformation program. The key shift is treating AI agents as autonomous contributors requiring structured context, rather than smart autocomplete tools requiring human oversight of every step. For enterprise leaders, this reframes the AI ROI conversation: the limiting factor is organizational and process change, not model capability. The caveat: the 10x claims reflect early-adopter frontier teams; most enterprise environments will face change management, security, and governance friction that moderates these gains significantly.",
