        "execSummary":  "This piece makes a foundational argument: AI security is an engineering discipline with defined requirements, enforceable controls, and clear accountability—not a policy afterthought. The emphasis on traceable agent identities and enforceable boundaries is directly relevant to enterprise deployments where agents are acting autonomously across systems and APIs. For security and operations leaders, the key implication is that agentic AI deployments require a new security architecture layer that traditional cybersecurity frameworks don\u0027t fully address. The caveat: NVIDIA frames this through an open-stack lens that implicitly advocates for their own ecosystem; the principles are sound, but implementation guidance will vary significantly by vendor stack.",
