        "execSummary":  "NVIDIA\u0027s article documents how the majority of frontier AI models—including OpenAI\u0027s latest GPT series—are trained on NVIDIA infrastructure, reinforcing NVIDIA\u0027s position as the foundational platform layer beneath the entire AI industry. The three-scaling-law framework (pretraining, post-training, test-time) is a useful lens for enterprise AI buyers to understand why model capability continues to advance and why infrastructure investment at the frontier translates into downstream capability gains in enterprise deployments. For enterprise leaders, the key implication is that NVIDIA\u0027s hardware dominance creates a durable platform dependency that shapes the competitive landscape for all AI vendors. The caveat: this is promotional content—the \u0027majority of models\u0027 claim is unverified by independent sources and should be treated as vendor positioning.",
