        "title":  "The 7 new Cs of IT leadership for the AI era",
        "source":  "CIO.com",
        "url":  "https://www.cio.com/article/4222994/the-7-new-cs-of-it-leadership-for-the-ai-era.html",
        "date":  "2026-09-17",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Dan Roberts presents seven essential leadership competencies for technology executives navigating AI-driven transformation: Coherence, Communication, Currency, Confidence, Conviction, Courage, and Change. These capabilities help leaders make sense of disruption, align organizational efforts, and accelerate business impact in an environment where change cycles are compressing rapidly. The seven competencies form a reinforcing flywheel where each builds upon the others.",
        "execSummary":  "Enterprise AI transformation is failing at the leadership layer, not the technology layer—CIOs who lack the \u0027seven Cs\u0027 will slow their organizations\u0027 ability to adapt and capture AI value. Roberts argues that coherence and conviction are the hardest to sustain because they require leaders to hold a clear direction amid constant change. For senior leaders, the takeaway is that AI strategy execution is inseparable from leadership development: investing in technical platforms without building these competencies produces fragile, stalled programs. The key caveat is that these competencies must be modeled from the top; delegating AI culture-building to middle management is a common and costly mistake.",
