        "date":  "2026-09-30",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "A BCG report reveals that 80% of AI spending now occurs outside IT budgets, with AI investment jumping from 1.7% to 3.3% of revenue. CIOs must adopt a \u0027chief integration officer\u0027 role, establishing visibility across distributed spending and connecting costs to measurable business outcomes rather than managing isolated projects.",
        "execSummary":  "AI spending has decisively escaped IT\u0027s perimeter—with four out of five AI dollars flowing through business-unit budgets, CIOs who lack cross-functional visibility are flying blind on both risk and return. The BCG data signal a structural shift: AI is now a revenue-line investment, not an IT cost, and governance models built around centralized approval are already obsolete. For enterprise leaders, the immediate priority is building a spend-mapping capability that ties distributed AI initiatives to business KPIs before duplication, shadow risk, and compliance gaps compound. The key watch item is that decentralized AI spending increases the probability of unmonitored models in production—a direct governance and regulatory exposure.",
        "vendorLean":  "Neutral",
        "imageUrl":  "https://imgproxy.divecdn.com/gGWrqlY9th7ZinbrWBLYgIiOiFpQcCu-D9P_94rZJ8c/g:ce/rs:fill:1200:675:1/Z3M6Ly9kaXZlc2l0ZS1zdG9yYWdlL2RpdmVpbWFnZS9HZXR0eUltYWdlcy0yMjA1MTE4MDI1LmpwZw==.webp",
